            "review_text": "rmwhitt44\nStamford, Connecticut110 contributions\n0\nView 5* but that's IT!\nMar 2025 • Friends\nREAD THE OTHER REVIEW. (1*) It's the EXACT SAME as our experience for the 4 of us, including the menu-sharing and drink-ordering experience! Service was haphazard at best---the staff (very young) was very disorganized and we could not identify our server (seems that staff is not assigned to wait on specific tables). One young man--poor guy!-- did his best to avoid eye contact with me when I was trying to get someone to take our drink orders--most of the staff doesn't speak English. \n\nFood was OK but brought out at different times--my friend and I were almost finished when they brought out the other two meals for our friends. My friend ordered Hot Pot and while the seafood was bountiful and good, the bok choy was dirty/uncleaned. \n\nBUT THE VIEW WAS INCREDIBLE. Tables on the 4th level of a big food complex with other restaurants overlooked the river, and we watched the Dragon Bridge show (9pm on Saturday/Sunday) from our table. \n\nBelow us was the Love Bridge (I think) where you can stand and watch the dragon breathe fire and water--so don't bother with this restaurant unless you want to have the same type of experience that we had.\nRead more\nInsider tip:\nDrink menu sucks too.\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten March 24, 2025",
